1
00:00:05,850 --> 00:00:11,454
A fishing village called Colachel, at the
southern tip of India.

2
00:00:11,554 --> 00:00:13,950
August, seventeen forty-one.

3
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:19,621
On the beach stands a wall of sharpened wooden
posts.

4
00:00:19,721 --> 00:00:24,002
Behind it wait the soldiers of the Dutch East
India Company,

5
00:00:24,102 --> 00:00:29,333
a trading company from the Netherlands with its
own ships, its own forts,

6
00:00:29,433 --> 00:00:30,575
and its own army.

7
00:00:32,475 --> 00:00:36,005
Outside the wall is the army of
Travancore,

8
00:00:36,105 --> 00:00:40,141
a small kingdom on the south-west coast of
India.

9
00:00:40,241 --> 00:00:42,504
Its king is Marthanda Varma.

10
00:00:42,604 --> 00:00:44,783
He is thirty-six years old.

11
00:00:46,683 --> 00:00:49,211
The Dutch came here to punish him.

12
00:00:49,311 --> 00:00:52,921
They have ships, cannons and trained
musketeers.

13
00:00:53,021 --> 00:00:58,950
Two years ago, their governor told this king
that the Company could crush him.

14
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:04,341
Now the Dutch are the ones who are
trapped.

15
00:01:04,441 --> 00:01:09,853
Behind them, the monsoon sea is too rough for
ships to come close.

16
00:01:09,953 --> 00:01:13,277
Inside the wall, the rice is running low.

17
00:01:13,377 --> 00:01:16,283
And the king outside is in no hurry.

18
00:01:18,183 --> 00:01:21,913
Soon, a single cannon shot will end this
siege.

19
00:01:22,013 --> 00:01:29,492
And the Dutch commander will spend the rest of
his life working for the king he came to beat.

20
00:01:29,592 --> 00:01:34,055
So, how did a trading company end up trapped on
a beach,

21
00:01:34,155 --> 00:01:36,907
a short march from a king's palace?

22
00:01:37,007 --> 00:01:38,700
It starts with pepper.

23
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:44,600
Kerala, the early seventeen hundreds.

24
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:48,700
Picture a map, with north at the top.

25
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:55,824
A long, thin strip of land runs down the west
coast of India.

26
00:01:55,924 --> 00:01:58,530
On one side is the Arabian Sea.

27
00:01:58,630 --> 00:02:04,029
On the other is a wall of green hills called
the Western Ghats.

28
00:02:04,129 --> 00:02:10,575
Between them, the land is wet, thick with
coconut palms, and cut by rivers.

29
00:02:12,475 --> 00:02:15,262
On those hills grows black pepper,

30
00:02:15,362 --> 00:02:19,933
a small dried berry that Europeans pay high
prices for.

31
00:02:20,033 --> 00:02:23,075
Ships have come for it for centuries.

32
00:02:24,975 --> 00:02:28,718
The coast is split into many small
kingdoms.

33
00:02:28,818 --> 00:02:35,356
Kochi, Kollam, Kayamkulam, and a crowd of tiny
ones, each with its own raja,

34
00:02:35,456 --> 00:02:36,492
a local king.

35
00:02:38,392 --> 00:02:41,006
The Dutch hold the fort at Kochi.

36
00:02:41,106 --> 00:02:45,613
They took it from the Portuguese in sixteen
sixty-three.

37
00:02:45,713 --> 00:02:48,492
On our map, Dutch forts are orange.

38
00:02:50,392 --> 00:02:52,383
Their method is simple.

39
00:02:52,483 --> 00:02:56,112
They sign contracts with the small rajas.

40
00:02:56,212 --> 00:02:59,931
Sell your pepper only to us, at our price.

41
00:03:00,031 --> 00:03:06,478
And because each raja is small, none of them is
strong enough to refuse.

42
00:03:06,578 --> 00:03:07,751
Remember that.

43
00:03:07,851 --> 00:03:14,117
The whole Dutch plan depends on the kings of
this coast staying small.

44
00:03:16,017 --> 00:03:21,508
Now look south, to the very tip of the
strip.

45
00:03:21,608 --> 00:03:24,117
Meet Marthanda Varma.

46
00:03:26,017 --> 00:03:28,606
He is born in seventeen oh-five.

47
00:03:28,706 --> 00:03:35,582
In seventeen twenty-nine, at about twenty-four,
he becomes the ruler of Travancore.

48
00:03:35,682 --> 00:03:41,214
His capital is Padmanabhapuram, a palace town
built of carved wood,

49
00:03:41,314 --> 00:03:44,492
about thirteen kilometres from the sea.

50
00:03:46,392 --> 00:03:47,947
Travancore is small.

51
00:03:48,047 --> 00:03:50,677
And his own nobles are not loyal.

52
00:03:50,777 --> 00:03:58,538
He spends his first years fighting powerful
families at home who do not want him on the throne.

53
00:03:58,638 --> 00:03:59,200
He wins.

54
00:04:01,100 --> 00:04:02,765
Then he turns north.

55
00:04:02,865 --> 00:04:08,941
In the seventeen thirties, his army takes one
neighbour after another.

56
00:04:09,041 --> 00:04:09,735
Attingal.

57
00:04:09,835 --> 00:04:12,470
The hill country of Nedumangad.

58
00:04:12,570 --> 00:04:13,617
Kottarakkara.

59
00:04:15,517 --> 00:04:18,562
And here is the problem for the Dutch.

60
00:04:18,662 --> 00:04:24,274
Each of those little kingdoms had signed a
pepper contract with them.

61
00:04:24,374 --> 00:04:29,075
Once the land belongs to Travancore, the
contract is gone.

62
00:04:29,175 --> 00:04:35,283
The pepper goes to whoever pays the most, and
often that means the English.

63
00:04:37,183 --> 00:04:41,339
The Dutch needed the kings to stay small.

64
00:04:41,439 --> 00:04:45,283
This one is getting bigger every year.

65
00:04:47,183 --> 00:04:52,078
So, in seventeen thirty-nine, the Dutch send an
important man.

66
00:04:52,178 --> 00:04:56,508
Meet Gustaaf Willem van Imhoff, the governor of
Ceylon,

67
00:04:56,608 --> 00:04:59,408
the island known today as Sri Lanka.

68
00:05:01,308 --> 00:05:05,311
Van Imhoff comes to Kochi to fix the pepper
problem.

69
00:05:05,411 --> 00:05:10,360
He writes that Dutch business on this coast is
in complete ruin.

70
00:05:10,460 --> 00:05:13,200
And he believes the answer is force.

71
00:05:15,100 --> 00:05:20,644
He demands that Marthanda Varma give back one
of the kingdoms he has taken,

72
00:05:20,744 --> 00:05:23,428
and return it to its exiled princess.

73
00:05:23,528 --> 00:05:27,492
If the king refuses, the Dutch will invade
Travancore.

74
00:05:29,392 --> 00:05:33,651
The king's answer has become a famous story in
Kerala.

75
00:05:33,751 --> 00:05:34,943
The historian M.

76
00:05:35,043 --> 00:05:35,104
O.

77
00:05:35,204 --> 00:05:37,364
Koshy recorded it like this.

78
00:05:37,464 --> 00:05:42,692
The king says that if the Dutch come, he will
go into the forests.

79
00:05:42,792 --> 00:05:46,567
Van Imhoff says the Dutch will follow him
there.

80
00:05:46,667 --> 00:05:52,783
And the king replies that he has been thinking
about invading Europe one day.

81
00:05:54,683 --> 00:06:01,203
The story has been told many ways, and it may
have grown in the telling.

82
00:06:01,303 --> 00:06:03,502
But the meaning is clear.

83
00:06:03,602 --> 00:06:05,617
The king is not afraid.

84
00:06:07,517 --> 00:06:08,734
Van Imhoff leaves.

85
00:06:08,834 --> 00:06:13,637
In November seventeen thirty-nine, the Dutch in
Kerala declare war.

86
00:06:13,737 --> 00:06:18,248
They do it without permission from their own
bosses in Batavia,

87
00:06:18,348 --> 00:06:22,200
the Company's capital in Asia, which is Jakarta
today.

88
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:26,904
At first, the war goes the Dutch way.

89
00:06:27,004 --> 00:06:32,399
The Dutch and their allies, the rajas of
Kollam, Kayamkulam and Kochi,

90
00:06:32,499 --> 00:06:35,617
march on the Travancore army near Kollam.

91
00:06:37,517 --> 00:06:42,243
An exploding shell lands on the Travancore
gunpowder store.

92
00:06:42,343 --> 00:06:43,224
It blows up.

93
00:06:43,324 --> 00:06:48,704
The Travancore soldiers run, and the Dutch
capture sixteen cannons.

94
00:06:48,804 --> 00:06:51,158
Remember that gunpowder store.

95
00:06:53,058 --> 00:06:56,605
The allies push south toward Attingal and
Varkala.

96
00:06:56,705 --> 00:07:02,657
But at Varkala they meet about five thousand
Nairs, the warrior families of Kerala,

97
00:07:02,757 --> 00:07:06,741
men trained to fight with sword and shield from
boyhood.

98
00:07:06,841 --> 00:07:10,533
The allies cannot break through, and they pull
back.

99
00:07:12,433 --> 00:07:18,341
So, for most of seventeen forty, the war in the
north goes back and forth.

100
00:07:18,441 --> 00:07:20,533
Neither side can finish it.

101
00:07:22,433 --> 00:07:24,729
Then, in late seventeen forty,

102
00:07:24,829 --> 00:07:30,800
the Dutch get about one hundred and
seventy-five fresh soldiers from Ceylon.

103
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:32,796
And they make a new plan.

104
00:07:32,896 --> 00:07:36,231
Stop fighting the king's army in the
north.

105
00:07:36,331 --> 00:07:38,867
Strike him at home, in the south.

106
00:07:40,767 --> 00:07:44,555
On the twenty-sixth of November, seventeen
forty,

107
00:07:44,655 --> 00:07:48,524
Dutch warships appear off the coast near
Colachel.

108
00:07:48,624 --> 00:07:50,349
They fire on the shore.

109
00:07:50,449 --> 00:07:54,158
Three days later, the Dutch announce a
blockade.

110
00:07:54,258 --> 00:07:57,492
No ship may trade with Travancore's coast.

111
00:07:59,392 --> 00:08:02,773
Then, in February seventeen forty-one,

112
00:08:02,873 --> 00:08:08,361
seven large ships and a crowd of smaller boats
come in close.

113
00:08:08,461 --> 00:08:13,492
Soldiers wade ashore on the sand just north of
Colachel.

114
00:08:15,392 --> 00:08:18,475
Meet their commander, Eustachius De
Lannoy.

115
00:08:18,575 --> 00:08:20,252
He is about twenty-five,

116
00:08:20,352 --> 00:08:26,174
a Catholic officer from a family of the
borderlands between France and Flanders.

117
00:08:26,274 --> 00:08:28,617
His speciality is building forts.

118
00:08:30,517 --> 00:08:32,327
Now look at the ground.

119
00:08:32,427 --> 00:08:36,647
Colachel is a fishing village on a long sandy
beach.

120
00:08:36,747 --> 00:08:40,136
Behind it are rice fields and palm groves.

121
00:08:40,236 --> 00:08:46,033
About thirteen kilometres inland is
Padmanabhapuram, the king's palace.

122
00:08:47,933 --> 00:08:51,952
On the beach, the Dutch build a stockade,

123
00:08:52,052 --> 00:08:56,975
a wall of thick wooden posts driven into the
sand.

124
00:08:57,075 --> 00:08:59,285
Then they march inland.

125
00:08:59,385 --> 00:09:04,408
Village after village falls, all the way to
Kottar.

126
00:09:06,308 --> 00:09:08,284
How big is their force?

127
00:09:08,384 --> 00:09:11,713
The records do not give a clear total.

128
00:09:11,813 --> 00:09:18,121
Perhaps a few hundred European soldiers, with
local troops beside them.

129
00:09:18,221 --> 00:09:19,835
It is a small army.

130
00:09:19,935 --> 00:09:25,160
But the king and most of his men are far away
in the north.

131
00:09:25,260 --> 00:09:28,950
And now the Dutch are close to his palace.

132
00:09:30,850 --> 00:09:32,913
Marthanda Varma rushes south.

133
00:09:33,013 --> 00:09:38,805
At Kalkulam, near his capital, he raises about
two thousand more Nair fighters,

134
00:09:38,905 --> 00:09:41,117
on top of his regular soldiers.

135
00:09:43,017 --> 00:09:45,631
Legend says that before the march,

136
00:09:45,731 --> 00:09:50,262
he goes to the temple of Adikesava Perumal at
Thiruvattar,

137
00:09:50,362 --> 00:09:52,976
and lays his sword before the god.

138
00:09:53,076 --> 00:09:59,283
Some accounts date the march to the
twenty-seventh of May, seventeen forty-one.

139
00:10:01,183 --> 00:10:03,283
Then the weather changes.

140
00:10:03,383 --> 00:10:06,801
In June, the south-west monsoon arrives.

141
00:10:06,901 --> 00:10:14,103
Heavy rain, strong winds, and a sea that throws
waves onto the beach day and night.

142
00:10:14,203 --> 00:10:19,117
For months, big ships cannot safely come near
this coast.

143
00:10:21,017 --> 00:10:24,326
Think about what that means for the Dutch.

144
00:10:24,426 --> 00:10:27,574
Their help is in Ceylon, across the sea.

145
00:10:27,674 --> 00:10:32,445
And their bosses in Batavia have a war of their
own in Java.

146
00:10:32,545 --> 00:10:33,825
No one is coming.

147
00:10:35,725 --> 00:10:40,144
The Travancore army pushes the Dutch out of the
villages.

148
00:10:40,244 --> 00:10:41,571
Back to the coast.

149
00:10:41,671 --> 00:10:44,742
Back behind the wooden wall at Colachel.

150
00:10:46,642 --> 00:10:49,650
Then the king does something simple.

151
00:10:49,750 --> 00:10:52,845
He surrounds the stockade, and waits.

152
00:10:52,945 --> 00:11:00,617
This is a siege: an army camps around a fort
and cuts it off until the men inside give up.

153
00:11:02,517 --> 00:11:06,011
The Dutch have one more problem.

154
00:11:06,111 --> 00:11:10,617
The people of the beach are against them.

155
00:11:12,517 --> 00:11:18,536
Colachel belongs to the Mukkuvar, a fishing
community of the southern coast.

156
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:22,723
De Lannoy himself later wrote an account of the
war.

157
00:11:22,823 --> 00:11:27,474
In it, the fishermen refuse Dutch bribes, delay
Dutch help,

158
00:11:27,574 --> 00:11:30,533
and lead Dutch soldiers the wrong way.

159
00:11:32,433 --> 00:11:34,864
Kerala tells one more story.

160
00:11:34,964 --> 00:11:42,096
The fishermen set up palm tree trunks on carts,
shaped and painted like cannons.

161
00:11:42,196 --> 00:11:47,700
From the sea, the Travancore army looks far
bigger than it is.

162
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:53,411
That story is still told today.

163
00:11:53,511 --> 00:11:57,700
No record from the time proves it.

164
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:04,204
Two small Dutch ships try to sail in with
help.

165
00:12:04,304 --> 00:12:10,408
The Travancore guns open fire, and the ships
turn back to sea.

166
00:12:12,308 --> 00:12:13,988
June becomes July.

167
00:12:14,088 --> 00:12:18,536
Inside the stockade, the men count their
rice.

168
00:12:18,636 --> 00:12:21,700
Outside, the rain keeps falling.

169
00:12:23,600 --> 00:12:26,725
The fifth of August, seventeen forty-one.

170
00:12:26,825 --> 00:12:32,075
A Travancore gun fires at the stockade, the
same as every other day.

171
00:12:33,975 --> 00:12:37,704
But this ball lands on a barrel of
gunpowder.

172
00:12:37,804 --> 00:12:39,066
The historian M.

173
00:12:39,166 --> 00:12:39,236
O.

174
00:12:39,336 --> 00:12:45,533
Koshy wrote that a burning hot shot hit the
gunpowder barrel, by accident.

175
00:12:47,433 --> 00:12:48,963
The barrel explodes.

176
00:12:49,063 --> 00:12:51,408
Fire spreads through the camp.

177
00:12:51,508 --> 00:12:53,120
The rice stores burn.

178
00:12:53,220 --> 00:12:56,950
Koshy wrote that the fire went on for two
days.

179
00:12:58,850 --> 00:13:00,391
You know this one.

180
00:13:00,491 --> 00:13:07,226
Near Kollam, a lucky shot into a gunpowder
store broke the Travancore army.

181
00:13:07,326 --> 00:13:10,325
Now a lucky shot breaks the Dutch.

182
00:13:12,225 --> 00:13:12,793
No food.

183
00:13:12,893 --> 00:13:14,379
Very little powder.

184
00:13:14,479 --> 00:13:15,131
No ships.

185
00:13:15,231 --> 00:13:22,310
The Dutch Company's own records say the
garrison surrendered on the seventh of August.

186
00:13:22,410 --> 00:13:26,151
In Kerala, the day is remembered as the
tenth.

187
00:13:26,251 --> 00:13:30,158
Historians still argue over which date is
right.

188
00:13:32,058 --> 00:13:36,038
About twenty-four Dutch officers are taken
prisoner,

189
00:13:36,138 --> 00:13:39,489
among them De Lannoy and his deputy,
Donadi.

190
00:13:39,589 --> 00:13:45,138
Some historians say the surrender terms
promised the Dutch safe passage,

191
00:13:45,238 --> 00:13:50,158
with their weapons, and that the king did not
keep that promise.

192
00:13:52,058 --> 00:14:00,158
The prisoners are marched inland to Udayagiri,
a fort in the hills near the capital.

193
00:14:02,058 --> 00:14:06,612
Now comes the strangest part of the story.

194
00:14:06,712 --> 00:14:10,158
The king offers De Lannoy a job.

195
00:14:12,058 --> 00:14:17,833
Train my army, he says, the way Europeans
fight.

196
00:14:17,933 --> 00:14:20,158
De Lannoy says yes.

197
00:14:22,058 --> 00:14:28,841
He drills the Travancore soldiers to fire
muskets in lines, and to work cannon.

198
00:14:28,941 --> 00:14:32,674
He sets up a works to make iron
cannonballs.

199
00:14:32,774 --> 00:14:39,033
He rebuilds the fort at Udayagiri, the same
fort where he was a prisoner.

200
00:14:40,933 --> 00:14:43,785
The king gives him a title.

201
00:14:43,885 --> 00:14:49,033
Valiya Kappithan, which means the Great
Captain.

202
00:14:50,933 --> 00:14:55,668
With his trained army, Travancore takes Kollam,
then Kayamkulam,

203
00:14:55,768 --> 00:14:57,330
and keeps going north.

204
00:14:57,430 --> 00:15:00,200
De Lannoy also designs the Nedumkotta,

205
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:05,110
a long line of walls and ditches across the
north of the kingdom.

206
00:15:05,210 --> 00:15:10,700
Decades later, those lines will stand in the
way of Tipu Sultan of Mysore.

207
00:15:12,600 --> 00:15:16,643
De Lannoy serves Travancore for about
thirty-seven years.

208
00:15:16,743 --> 00:15:19,187
He dies in seventeen seventy-seven,

209
00:15:19,287 --> 00:15:23,330
and he is buried in a small chapel inside
Udayagiri fort.

210
00:15:23,430 --> 00:15:25,075
His tomb is still there.

211
00:15:26,975 --> 00:15:29,533
The war does not end at Colachel.

212
00:15:29,633 --> 00:15:33,882
The Dutch hold Kanyakumari, the southern tip of
India,

213
00:15:33,982 --> 00:15:37,909
until October seventeen forty-one, and then
leave.

214
00:15:38,009 --> 00:15:40,325
Peace talks drag on for years.

215
00:15:42,225 --> 00:15:47,335
In seventeen fifty-three, the two sides sign
the Treaty of Mavelikkara.

216
00:15:47,435 --> 00:15:50,930
The Dutch promise not to stand in the king's
way.

217
00:15:51,030 --> 00:15:54,158
They even agree to sell him guns and
powder.

218
00:15:56,058 --> 00:15:57,849
Remember the Dutch plan?

219
00:15:57,949 --> 00:16:01,631
It needed the kings of this coast to stay
small.

220
00:16:01,731 --> 00:16:07,146
After Colachel, Marthanda Varma becomes the
biggest king on the coast,

221
00:16:07,246 --> 00:16:10,533
and the pepper trade passes into his
hands.

222
00:16:12,433 --> 00:16:15,847
In seventeen fifty, he does something
unusual.

223
00:16:15,947 --> 00:16:18,978
He gives his whole kingdom to Padmanabha,

224
00:16:19,078 --> 00:16:22,798
the god of the great temple at
Thiruvananthapuram,

225
00:16:22,898 --> 00:16:26,158
and rules from then on as the god's
servant.

226
00:16:28,058 --> 00:16:32,195
Today, a victory pillar stands on the beach at
Colachel.

227
00:16:32,295 --> 00:16:39,458
The Indian Army's Madras Regiment traces part
of its history to the Nair soldiers of Travancore.

228
00:16:39,558 --> 00:16:45,283
And at the army camp at Pangode, the parade
ground is called Kulachal Ground.

229
00:16:47,183 --> 00:16:50,200
So, why did the Dutch lose at Colachel?

230
00:16:50,300 --> 00:16:52,997
A small force landed far from home.

231
00:16:53,097 --> 00:16:55,874
The monsoon cut it off from the sea.

232
00:16:55,974 --> 00:16:58,831
The fishing people worked against it.

233
00:16:58,931 --> 00:17:02,507
A patient king starved it inside its own
wall.

234
00:17:02,607 --> 00:17:05,783
And one burning shot found the gunpowder.

235
00:17:07,683 --> 00:17:08,252
In India,

236
00:17:08,352 --> 00:17:14,125
Colachel is often called the first time an
Asian kingdom beat a European power.

237
00:17:14,225 --> 00:17:15,760
That claim is too big.

238
00:17:15,860 --> 00:17:20,220
The Mughals had already beaten the Portuguese,
and in China,

239
00:17:20,320 --> 00:17:24,605
Koxinga drove the Dutch out of Taiwan in
sixteen sixty-two.

240
00:17:24,705 --> 00:17:27,207
But Colachel did something unusual.

241
00:17:27,307 --> 00:17:29,883
It ended Dutch plans for this coast,

242
00:17:29,983 --> 00:17:34,492
and it turned the enemy commander into the
king's own general.

243
00:17:36,392 --> 00:17:37,083
A beach.

244
00:17:37,183 --> 00:17:38,469
A wooden wall.

245
00:17:38,569 --> 00:17:41,439
One shot into a powder barrel.

246
00:17:41,539 --> 00:17:46,783
And a Dutch captain who stayed for thirty-seven
years.

